From 309c88f3c04a798d938bbc98145c3bd386999487 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 22:35:20 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-37: with several selected, the properties panel
 changes every one of them (0.37.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WPF's property grid sets a value on every selected control. Now so does ours:
with a multi-selection, a change in 外觀與版面 (font, bold, colours, caption,
Left / Width ...) goes to all of them as ONE source edit = one undo step.
The panel shows the primary's values and says so (note + section title
"套用到全部 N 個"). Position / size is all or nothing: one locked or not
movable = none changes, the status bar says why. A caption skips the ones
that have none (and says how many). The HTML source rows stay primary-only.

- probe: layoutPlan (the old setLayout checks, now reusable) + editAllSel;
  setLayout / setCaption / setLook with all: true and the key of the
  current primary use it, anything else keeps the old single path
- host: forwardEdit passes all when the panel's data has a multi-selection
- tests: probe (bold + width on 2 = one batch each, a locked one = none,
  without all = primary only, the multi-selection kept), smoke (all: true
  only with 2 selected), panels_render (note + title), real VS Code
  (italic on sbtExit + spbSave in the source, ONE undo, no save)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
